//? Title: Rounding rules: actual half-integer decisions and sample-specific signed error
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Map observations to integer-valued outputs with an explicit tie rule and measure
the observed rounding error. Integer rounding differs at represented
half-integers and in directed modes. The native producer now classifies original
fractions before deciding ties and captures actual per-value errors. The
original six scalar examples and 60 positive ties remain, with adjacent-float
controls.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Write x=floor(x)+r. For a nearest-integer rule, r<1/2 chooses the lower integer
and r>1/2 the upper; only r=1/2 invokes the tie rule. The producer uses a
widened input-minus-floor difference so addition of1/2 does not round before
classification.
$$ e_i=R(x_i)-x_i,\qquad \bar e_n=\frac1n\sum_{i=1}^{n}e_i. $$
\alttext(The actual signed sample error is rounded output minus input, averaged in widened arithmetic.)
A mean error is descriptive for the supplied sample. Half-to-even balances
alternating parity ties in this particular 60-value fixture; it is not unbiased
for every possible population. Scalar NaN/infinities propagate, but error
summaries require finite samples.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/rounding_functions_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = a::rounding_trace({.5, 1.5, -.5, -1.5}, a::RoundMode::HalfToEven);
    std::print("| input | widened fraction | actual tie | rounded | error | running mean |\n| ---: | ---: | " "--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.input, s.fraction,
                   s.tie, s.rounded, s.error, s.mean_error);
    g::Diagram d(48, 1100);
    d.node("n0", {0, 0}, std::format("Actual input {}", t.steps[0].input));
    d.node("n1", {5, 0}, std::format("Actual tie {}", t.steps[0].tie));
    d.node("n2", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual output {}, error {}", t.steps[0].rounded,
                       t.steps[0].error));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/rounding_functions_tiny.svg");
}
```
